  "explanation": "The question asks for the modern-day name(s) of Abdera. From the original sources:\n\n- D1S1 explicitly states that 'Abdera was an ancient Carthaginian and Roman port on a hill above the modern Adra on the southeastern Mediterranean coast of Spain.' This directly supports 'Adra' as a modern-day name.\n\n- D5S4 states that 'The present-day town is written Avdira and pronounced in modern Greek.' This supports 'Avdira' as a modern-day name in Greece.\n\nBoth 'Adra' and 'Avdira' are distinct referents referring to modern-day locations associated with ancient Abdera (one in Spain, one in Greece). These are complementary answers, not conflicting, and both are supported by direct statements in the original sources."
